\contentsline {todo}{\fcolorbox {black}{orange}{\textcolor {orange}{o}}\ Expand. The acquisition-grouped, twin-merged evaluation holds out operating-point groups, but because the (RPM, temperature) space is densely and smoothly sampled, every held-out group is surrounded by near-neighbour training points. The high $R^2$ therefore reflects \emph {interpolation} of the smooth $\kappa $(operating-point) surface---consistent with the operating-point soft-sensor interpretation---rather than \emph {extrapolation} to new regimes. Same-operating-point leakage is controlled, but generalisation to unsampled operating regimes (or to independently varied lubricant state) is untested; the excluded sub-floor cold-start sweeps illustrate the extrapolation failure mode.}{28}{section*.36}%
